outputs.exact_statement:
One has $0<m_*<\infty$. At separated Euclidean points, the like-component two-point function is the continuous kernel $$C(t,b)=\int\rho(d\mu^2)\int_{\mathbb R}\frac{dp}{2\pi}
          \frac{e^{ipb-tE(p,\mu)}}{2E(p,\mu)},
 \qquad E(p,\mu)=\sqrt{p^2+\mu^2},\quad t>0.
 \label{inp:euclidean}$$ It is strictly positive at every nonzero Euclidean separation, and there is a constant $C_0$ such that $$0<C(t,b)\le C_0e^{-m_*\sqrt{t^2+b^2}}
 \quad\text{when }\sqrt{t^2+b^2}\ge1.
 \label{inp:decay}$$

On the even subspace perpendicular to the vacuum, $$\label{par:even-norm}
          \bigl\|T\big|_{\mathrm{even}\cap\Omega^\perp}\bigr\|
                         \le\tau^2.$$ There is a real unit $\tau$-eigenfunction $\psi$ that is odd under simultaneous spin inversion and, after a component permutation, odd under the reflection of component $3$ alone. It satisfies $$\label{par:overlap}
                    \langle \Omega,|\psi|\rangle^2\ge\frac{\tau}{1+\tau}.$$

The probability that an open cluster meets both the row at time $0$ and the row at time $d$ satisfies $$\label{vis:row-connection}
 \mathbb P_{\mathrm{tor}}(0\longleftrightarrow d)
       \ge c\,e^{-(d+a)e_N(w)}.$$

There is a constant $C$ such that, for every sufficiently large dyadic circumference $w=w_k$, $$\label{cou:linear-eq}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}\mathcal N_{N,w}(u_0)\le Cw,
 \qquad u_0=\frac32m_*.$$

For all sufficiently large $w$, uniformly in $y\in[u_0,u_1]$, $$\begin{aligned}
 Q_{w,y}(e^{-E})&\ge1-Ce^{-cD^{3/4}}
       &&(0\le E\le y),\label{cou:poly-low}\\
 Q_{w,y}(e^{-E})&\le Ce^{-cD^{3/4}}e^{-t_0E}
       &&(E\ge y+b_w).\label{cou:poly-high}
\end{aligned}$$ Every nonzero monomial of $Q_{w,y}$ has degree between $t_0$ and $D$, and the sum of the absolute values of its coefficients is at most $3^D$.

For every integer $n\ge0$ and every compact interval $I$ with nonempty interior, $$\label{mass:moments-eq}
 \lim_{\substack{w\to\infty\\w=w_k}}\limsup_{N\to\infty}
 \max_{p\in I}
 \left|
   \int x^n\,\nu_{N,w,p}(dx)
   -\int_\mathbb Re^{-ipb}C_f(n,b)\,db
 \right|=0.$$
